  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employment for young men and women through promotion of entrepreneurship, access to BDS, LED/LER and sustainable livelihoods initiatives.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2021, the Revised National Development Strategy (2021-2024) acknowledged the role of minimum wage in poverty reduction and the Decent Work Country Programme adopted in October 2023 highlighted the importance of ensuring &#x201c;that all workers enjoy adequate protection in accordance with the Decent Work Agenda, taking into account respect for their fundamental rights; an adequate minimum wage, statutory or negotiated; maximum limits on working time; and safety and health at work&#x201d;. 
In February 2024, following the request from the Government of South Sudan, ILO initiated activities to start the processes for setting up minimum wage for the Country. In this regard, a two-day workshop has been organized by the ILO on establishing a sustainable minimum wage system in South Sudan. It brought together representatives from various stakeholders, including government officials, employers, workers&apos; representatives, and Developmental partners. Key discussions revolved around wage policies, international labour standards, and the challenges faced in South Sudan, including issues related to inflation, lack of employment opportunities, and payment delays. Participants reached a consensus on the importance of setting a minimum wage and agreed on a roadmap for the coming months that includes the building of institutions, research and capacity building activities. 
Output 6.2. Increased capacity of Member States to set adequate wages and promote decent working time
The CPO SSD103 envisages to support the government and social partners to come up with a minimum wage system for South Sudan. The strategy will focus on building technical capacity of the concerned stakeholders, conducting assessments and sharing good practices in the areas as well as creating awareness and knowledge on the subject are critical.
The CPO also aims at supporting the government of South Sudan to develop a labour migration policy for improved governance of labour migration.
